## overview — Overview
Host vitals, container counts, project health, the biggest memory users and recent warnings. Call this first.
  {
    "additionalProperties": false,
    "type": "object"
  }

## query_metrics — Query metrics
Summary statistics (min, max, avg, p95, last) for metrics of one entity over the last minutes; raw points on request. Metrics: cpu.util, mem.used_bytes, mem.used_ratio, net.rx_bps, net.tx_bps, load.1 (host), blk.read_bps, blk.write_bps, pids.count.
  {
    "additionalProperties": false,
    "properties": {
      "entity_id": {
        "description": "host (default) or a workload id such as ctr:shop-api-1",
        "type": "string"
      },
      "metrics": {
        "description": "metric names (default cpu.util and mem.used_bytes)",
        "items": {
          "type": "string"
        },
        "type": [
          "null",
          "array"
        ]
      },
      "raw": {
        "description": "also return the points, downsampled to at most 500",
        "type": "boolean"
      },
      "window": {
        "description": "how far back, e.g. 5m or 15m (default 15m, maximum 15m)",
        "type": "string"
      }
    },
    "type": "object"
  }

## tail_logs — Tail logs
Recent log lines for one workload (newest last), with optional substring filter. Obvious secrets are redacted.
  {
    "additionalProperties": false,
    "properties": {
      "before": {
        "description": "RFC 3339 time; return lines older than this (use next_before from a previous call to page back)",
        "type": "string"
      },
      "grep": {
        "description": "only lines containing this substring (case-insensitive)",
        "type": "string"
      },
      "limit": {
        "description": "lines to return, 1-500 (default 100)",
        "maximum": 4294967295,
        "minimum": 0,
        "type": "integer"
      },
      "workload_id": {
        "description": "workload or container id, e.g. ctr:shop-api-1",
        "type": "string"
      }
    },
    "required": [
      "workload_id"
    ],
    "type": "object"
  }

## top — Top workloads
The workloads using the most CPU or memory right now.
  {
    "additionalProperties": false,
    "properties": {
      "limit": {
        "description": "how many workloads, 1-50 (default 10)",
        "maximum": 4294967295,
        "minimum": 0,
        "type": "integer"
      },
      "metric": {
        "description": "cpu (default) or memory",
        "type": "string"
      }
    },
    "type": "object"
  }

